In a release that includes it, the terminal UI, supertag-tui, embeds OpenTUI's native library
(libopentui, from the @opentui/core-PLATFORM 0.9.4 packages, https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui;
MIT). That library statically links a decode-only build of FFmpeg 9.0.2 (https://ffmpeg.org),
licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later, and zlib. OpenTUI's
package also carries the licenses of the other components it names (Ghostty, Yoga, libwebp,
lcms2, stb, wuffs, gdtoa, Zig, LLVM, and others). Those licenses, and FFMPEG-SOURCE.md, which
names the exact FFmpeg source and its SHA-256, are in licenses/opentui/ of such a release archive.
FFmpeg's source is available from https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz, and OpenTUI's
source and build scripts, which rebuild and relink libopentui with a modified FFmpeg, from
https://github.com/anomalyco/opentui. supertag-tui loads a replacement library from the file that
OPENTUI_LIB_PATH names.
